// TEST: Tuple Width Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3001
// A `Tuple<N>` annotation lowers to an IRTTuple of N fresh element variables,
// so the width check is unify's existing equal-length IRTTuple rule
// (Unify.fs) rather than a new diagnostic: a 2-tuple value against a
// `Tuple<3>` slot is an ordinary type mismatch.
//
// This is the property Design C's substitution law rests on -- the width of a
// tuple-typed name is STATIC, so `f(a, t)` and `f(a, (b, c))` can be made to
// agree by the width-schema matcher (the next stage). If a width mismatch
// were tolerated here, pack widths would be inference-dependent and the
// matcher would have nothing to slice on.

let b = 1.0
let c = 2.0
let t: Tuple<3> = b, c
// EXPECT: typecheck failure -- a 2-wide value cannot fill a Tuple<3> slot
